      "title": {
        "en": "Mixed commentary on veterinary clinic staff"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Client reviews show diverging opinions regarding clinic staff at this Petco location on South Shepherd Drive. Many pet owners speak highly of Dr. Medina and veterinary assistants, highlighting friendly greetings and thorough medical attention. However, several dissatisfied clients report encounters with dismissive reception personnel, perceived bedside manner issues, and inconsistent client support."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle and patient pet handling"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet owners consistently note that veterinary technicians and assistants handle dogs and cats with care and warmth during exams and vaccination visits. Multiple clients mention that staff members help calm nervous puppies and take time to comfort frightened kittens. Except for an isolated complaint regarding an anxious dog, reviewers appreciate the gentle care shown to companion animals."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 10,
      "title": {
        "en": "Clear explanations balanced by communication gaps"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers share mixed feedback regarding communication before, during, and after clinic visits. Many owners praise practitioners for explaining treatment plans clearly and answering all questions without rushing. Conversely, several clients reported significant frustration with phone communication, citing difficulties receiving updates after vaccine reactions and feeling unheard by staff."
      }
    }
  ],
